WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
New Air assigned a 20-year gas PPA to power a 250 megawatts data center in Texas from an adjacent plant. Welcome to the very first episode of AI Chips &amp; Data Centres Daily. Today is September 22nd, 2026. This program follows the hardware that runs AI. It tracks the chips, the systems that hold them, and the data centers with their power and cooling needs. The main measure is gigawatts of capacity moving from announcement through construction to operation.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.680
Models and software sit with the sister show, models and agents.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.560
The focus stays on the physical build, the supply chain, and the money behind it.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.340
New era signed the agreement with a Vistro subsidiary.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.540
The data center sits in Ector County with the plant located in Odessa.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.200
The contract ties generation directly to the site load.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.800
It meets the full requirement without drawing on grid cues.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.740
No energization date appears in the release.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:02.700
The term gives the operator long-term visibility on both price and supply.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:09.940
Coherent Corporation announced the PhotonLink Integrated Optics Platform on September 22, 2026.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.340
The platform combines the company's broad portfolio of critical photonics technologies

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.700
with precision assembly and test capabilities.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.480
It is designed to deliver complete optical solutions for next-generation AI data centers.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:30.280
PhotonLink supports co-packaged optics, near-packaged optics, and emerging chip-to-chip connectivity.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.860
The announcement was made from Sachsenburg, Pennsylvania.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.380
It positions the offering for immediate use in high-density AI clusters.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:47.380
Global Unichip announced a 2nm HBM4EPHY and controller IP running at 16GB per second.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:53.920
The IP has been adopted in customer AI ASICS. It is positioned as design ready for advanced

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.400
packaging flows that pair high bandwidth memory with leading edge logic dies.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.220
The 16 gigabits per second data rate targets the next generation of memory interfaces beyond

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:10.580
current HBM3E deployments. No specific customer names or shipment volumes were disclosed.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:16.460
Cypherl delivered the first RIO-1 CPU samples to Bull for the Jupiter supercomputer.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:22.000
The ARM-based processor targets sovereign high-performance computing and AI workloads.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.860
The delivery marks the first silicon milestone for the European processor initiative spin-off.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.780
Bull will integrate the samples into the Jupiter system build.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:38.080
The RIO-1 design emphasizes energy-efficient operation for large-scale European installations.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:45.120
Green Data Center development is advancing plans for a 200 megawatts data center in Schladen-Verla, Germany.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.900
The project remains in the planning phase with no construction start data announced.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.300
The 200 megawatts capacity figure represents the target IT load for the facility.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.180
Local permitting and grid studies are understood to be underway.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.420
No tenant or power source details were released.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:09.300
Polcom will build a 40 megawatts data center in Skawina, Poland, as its second facility in the town.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.860
The new site adds to an existing Polcom presence and expands local cloud capacity.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.640
The 40 megawatts rating covers the planned IT load.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.880
Construction timing and exact power arrangements were not specified.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.920
The project supports enterprise and cloud workloads in the region.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:32.780
The program targets equipment intended for AI factories built to the DSX Blueprint.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:38.740
Vendors can submit power and cooling systems for qualification against NVIDIA defined performance

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.640
and interoperability criteria.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:46.980
The initiative aims to accelerate deployment of compliant infrastructure for large-scale AI clusters.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.440
No specific hardware vendors or qualification timelines were listed in the announcement.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:59.580
TSMC is building an advanced packaging validation hub in Kaohsiung in addition to capacity expansion.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.000
The hub focuses on process development and qualification rather than volume production.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:10.800
It supports ongoing work on advanced packaging technologies used for AI accelerators.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:18.320
The Kaohsiung location complements existing packaging sites and allows faster iteration on new interposer and bonding flows.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.260
No capital expenditure or completion date was disclosed.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.460
UBS raised its COWAS capacity forecast

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.580
after reviewing current demand signals.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.680
The updated projection shows

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:33.100
2027 demand nearly double this year's level.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.580
The increase reflects stronger orders

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.440
from AI accelerator suppliers

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.780
and their packaging partners.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.480
COWAS remains the dominant advanced

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.520
packaging technology for high-end GPUs and custom ASICs.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.100
No absolute wafer or unit numbers were provided in the forecast summary.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.060
ASC technology outlined a $10.5 billion capital expenditure plan aimed at AI demand.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.200
The multi-year spend targets advanced packaging capacity and technology development.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.520
It is intended to increase the company's ability to handle larger interposers and higher

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.520
volumes of AI-related assemblies.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.160
The plan aligns with industry-wide efforts to relieve packaging bottlenecks.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.360
No year-by-year breakdown or specific technology nodes were detailed.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.780
Take it apart and the limits on co-os throughput start with the number of usable interposer

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.080
reticles per 300 millimeters wafer.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:33.340
One wafer yield 70 to 90 reticle fields, each supporting one large GPU plus HBM stack.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:40.760
Current lines across suppliers process 8,000 to 12,000 wafer per month, which equals 600,000

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.980
to 1 million packaged units a year before yield losses.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:51.420
Adding a second bonding layer for larger interposers cuts effective throughput by 25-35% due

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.040
to longer alignment and thermal compression steps.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:06:01.460
The 2027 demand forecast nearly doubling from 2026 therefore requires either new clean

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:06.020
room bays or a shift to 510 millimeters panels still in pilot.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:11.500
The trade-off flips only when those panel lines reach volume production and ease allocation

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.300
pressure on accelerator shipments.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:18.240
In Vidya RTX 60 series parts are reported for 2028.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:27.360
Manufacturers are planning 4GB and 6GB GDDR7 chips for the 2027 to 2028 window.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:33.220
Alibaba has slated the Genwoo V900 for the first quarter of 2027.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:40.800
Before we go, TSMC's new validation hub in Kaushung begins qualifying interposer and bonding flows.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.920
That's AI chips and data centers for today.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.720
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.960
Thanks for listening. See you tomorrow.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.080
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.140
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
